{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-48910","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-93192","text":"Upstream RFC 8785 reference vectors — COMPLETE for the applicable suite"}]},{"id":"blk-48911","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93193","marks":["code"],"text":"input/<name>.json"},{"id":"spn-93194","text":" is fed to the canonicaliser; the result must equal the octets in "},{"id":"spn-93195","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex/<name>.txt"},{"id":"spn-93196","text":", which is ASCII hexadecimal."}]},{"id":"blk-48912","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-93197","text":"Provenance"}]},{"id":"blk-48913","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"repository   github.com/cyberphone/json-canonicalization\npath         testdata/\ncommit       19d51d7fe467d4706a3ff08adf8a748f29fc21e0   (2024-12-13)"},{"id":"blk-48914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93198","text":"All six vectors of the upstream "},{"id":"spn-93199","marks":["code"],"text":"testdata/input/"},{"id":"spn-93200","text":" set are present: "},{"id":"spn-93201","marks":["code"],"text":"arrays"},{"id":"spn-93202","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93203","marks":["code"],"text":"french"},{"id":"spn-93204","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93205","marks":["code"],"text":"structures"},{"id":"spn-93206","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93207","marks":["code"],"text":"unicode"},{"id":"spn-93208","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93209","marks":["code"],"text":"values"},{"id":"spn-93210","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93211","marks":["code"],"text":"weird"},{"id":"spn-93212","text":". "},{"id":"spn-93213","marks":["code"],"text":"values"},{"id":"spn-93214","text":" is also RFC 8785 sections 3.2.2 / 3.2.3 verbatim."}]},{"id":"blk-48915","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-93215","text":"Why "},{"id":"spn-93216","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex"},{"id":"spn-93217","text":" and not "},{"id":"spn-93218","marks":["code"],"text":"output"}]},{"id":"blk-48916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93219","text":"P4.3 and P4.4 could not import "},{"id":"spn-93220","marks":["code"],"text":"weird"},{"id":"spn-93221","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-93222","marks":["code"],"text":"unicode"},{"id":"spn-93223","text":" because their expected output contains unescaped U+0080, U+007F and a combining mark, and no text channel available to this tree could be shown to have preserved them byte for byte. "},{"id":"spn-93224","marks":["bold"],"text":"A conformance vector that might be wrong is worse than one that is narrow"},{"id":"spn-93225","text":", so they were declared open rather than guessed."}]},{"id":"blk-48917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93226","text":"Upstream publishes "},{"id":"spn-93227","marks":["code"],"text":"testdata/outhex/"},{"id":"spn-93228","text":", which states the expected canonical output as ASCII hexadecimal. That is the transport-safe representation the problem needed, and it is a strictly better test boundary than comparing decoded text: the comparison is against octets."}]},{"id":"blk-48918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93229","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex/{arrays,unicode,weird}.txt"},{"id":"spn-93230","text":" are upstream verbatim. "},{"id":"spn-93231","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex/{french,structures,values}.txt"},{"id":"spn-93232","text":" are the hex of the "},{"id":"spn-93233","marks":["code"],"text":"output/*.json"},{"id":"spn-93234","text":" files imported at P4.3, kept so that "},{"id":"spn-93235","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-93236","text":" vector is compared as octets rather than some as text."}]},{"id":"blk-48919","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-93237","text":"Why the inputs carry "},{"id":"spn-93238","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u"},{"id":"spn-93239","text":" escapes"}]},{"id":"blk-48920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93240","marks":["code"],"text":"input/weird.json"},{"id":"spn-93241","text":" upstream contains literal "},{"id":"spn-93242","marks":["code"],"text":"€"},{"id":"spn-93243","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93244","marks":["code"],"text":"😂"},{"id":"spn-93245","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93246","marks":["code"],"text":"ö"},{"id":"spn-93247","text":" and a Hebrew letter. Those are re-expressed here as "},{"id":"spn-93248","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u20ac"},{"id":"spn-93249","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93250","marks":["code"],"text":"\\ud83d\\ude02"},{"id":"spn-93251","text":", "},{"id":"spn-93252","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u00f6"},{"id":"spn-93253","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-93254","marks":["code"],"text":"\\ufb33"},{"id":"spn-93255","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-93256","marks":["bold"],"text":"the same JSON value"},{"id":"spn-93257","text":", since an escape and a literal denote one string, and transport-safe. The code points were read from the authoritative "},{"id":"spn-93258","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex"},{"id":"spn-93259","text":" bytes rather than from a rendering of the file, and the round trip is what proves them: if a single escape were wrong the canonical output would not equal the upstream octets. "},{"id":"spn-93260","marks":["code"],"text":"input/unicode.json"},{"id":"spn-93261","text":" already used escapes upstream."}]},{"id":"blk-48921","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-93262","text":"What is established, and what is not"}]},{"id":"blk-48922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93263","text":"Six vectors covering member ordering by UTF-16 code unit (including an empty key, numeric-looking keys, a surrogate pair that must sort before U+FB33, and an escaped newline as a key), ECMAScript number serialisation, string escaping, unescaped C1 controls and U+007F, combining marks preserved without normalisation, and array/structure nesting."}]},{"id":"blk-48923","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-93264","text":"This is the whole of upstream "},{"id":"spn-93265","marks":["code"],"text":"testdata/input/"},{"id":"spn-93266","text":". It is "},{"id":"spn-93267","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-93268","text":" the ~100M-case ECMAScript number stress corpus that project also publishes, and that remains a separately described strengthening target rather than a silent omission."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierahvjkl2jgazfr2g4xepdognvsyam27v6wrp2lf43kpr5y4b3lr4la","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}